# Qumbra T0 internal-net host spec (M10-T0-3). One node per line:
#
#   <node_name>   <public_addr host:port>   <ssh_target | ->   [miner_rkm]
#
# - public_addr : the address PEERS dial (a routable host:port). Used to build
#                 every other node's dial-peer list.
# - ssh_target  : user@host for rsync/ssh deploy, or "-" for LOCAL mode
#                 (dry-run — the payload is copied into <local-base>/<node_name>).
# - miner_rkm   : per host (lab #475). The 64-hex coinbase payee that node mines
#                 to — `qumbra-wallet miner-rkm --dir DIR` prints it.
#
#                 🔴 REQUIRED ON EVERY HOST OF A MINING FLEET, which is what
#                 `deploy.sh` generates by default. Since lab #552 (PR #655)
#                 `qumbra-node` REFUSES TO START with `mining = true` and no
#                 `miner_rkm` — every coin such a node mined was paid to a key
#                 nobody holds — so `deploy.sh` refuses to GENERATE that, naming
#                 every keyless host before it builds anything. Omit the column,
#                 or write "-", ONLY for a fleet deployed with `--no-mining` (a
#                 verify-only rehearsal): that flag is the one honest way to say
#                 "this fleet does not mine". The tool will not flip a keyless
#                 host to mining = false on its own — which hosts mine, and to
#                 what, is decided here, by you, per row.
#
#                 🔴 THIS FILE IS THE SOURCE OF TRUTH FOR THAT FIELD. Before the
#                 column existed, `deploy.sh` emitted no `miner_rkm` at all, so
#                 every re-run dropped it from the hosts that had one and the
#                 field had to be hand-restored on each host after every deploy
#                 (the standing 🔴 of OPERATOR §9.5.1). Edit it here; never on a
#                 host, where the next deploy overwrites it.
#
# The T0 net is fixed at N_machines = 4 (allows a 2+2 partition). The 21 committee
# keys split 6/5/5/5 across these 4 nodes in listed order.
#
# ---- real 4-VPS deploy (fill in for Phase B) --------------------------------
# AS SHIPPED THIS FILE IS A --no-mining TEMPLATE: no row carries a key, so
# `deploy.sh --hosts` REFUSES it until you either pass --no-mining or fill the
# 4th column on all four rows with your own `qumbra-wallet miner-rkm` output.
# No illustrative key is shipped, on purpose: a placeholder that reached a host
# is structurally valid, mines, and pays a key nobody holds — the same class of
# value as the payee on T2 blocks 607/610/611 (lab #552), and no refusal
# anywhere would catch it. A mining row looks like:
#
#   node1   203.0.113.11:9444    root@203.0.113.11   <the 64 hex characters `qumbra-wallet miner-rkm --dir DIR` printed>
node0   203.0.113.10:9444    root@203.0.113.10   -
node1   203.0.113.11:9444    root@203.0.113.11   -
node2   203.0.113.12:9444    root@203.0.113.12   -
node3   203.0.113.13:9444    root@203.0.113.13   -
